   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The function q is given by q(x) = 7 - x^2 for x < 1, q(x) = ax + b for 1 <= x <= 4, and q(x) = 4sqrt(x) + a for x > 4, where a and b are constants. If q is continuous for all real x, what is the value of a?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 1
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At x = 1 the left branch gives 7 - 1 = 6 and the middle branch gives a + b, so a + b = 6.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Add",
               "a",
               "b"
            ],
            6
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At x = 4 the middle branch gives 4a + b and the right branch gives 4sqrt(4) + a = 8 + a, so 4a + b = 8 + a, which is 3a + b = 8.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  3,
                  "a"
               ],
               "b"
            ],
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Subtracting the first equation from the second gives 2a = 2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "a"
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So a = 1, and b = 5.",
         "mathjson": 1
      }
